29:["$","div",null,{"className":"ms-body","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"prose","children":[["$","h2","h2-0",{"id":"why","children":"Why"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":"PM work dies in the gap between “I need user signal” and eight open tabs of Hacker News, Reddit and app-store reviews. A manual sweep takes days, and most of it is dedup work."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"id":"the-mechanism","children":"The mechanism"}],"\n",["$","div","p-1",{"className":"mp","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":["A four-step wizard captures the brief: topic, objective, audience, competitors, timeframe. Gemini plans the research from that brief — per-platform keywords, app hints, timeframes — then ",["$","mark","0",{"className":"mk","children":"parallel fetchers hit the live APIs (Hacker News, Reddit, App Store, Play Store, GitHub, Google Trends, Product Hunt, YouTube)"}],". SQL stages clean and deduplicate the corpus, an LLM pass labels each record into insight buckets with sentiment, and the output is a fixed-format User Insights Report — snapshot, buckets, evidence, trend, competitor comparison, methodology — as shareable markdown."]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mnotes","role":"note","children":[["$","span","The brief",{"className":"mnote","children":["$25:props:children:0",["$","b",null,{"children":"The brief"}],["$","i",null,{"children":"topic, objective, audience, competitors, timeframe"}]]}],["$","span","The engine",{"className":"mnote","children":["$25:props:children:0",["$","b",null,{"children":"The engine"}],["$","i",null,{"children":"Gemini plans the research from that brief"}]]}]]}]]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-2",{"id":"budget-and-guardrails","children":"Budget and guardrails"}],"\n",["$","div","p-2",{"className":"mp","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":["Strictly ",["$","mark","0",{"className":"mk","children":"≤3 Gemini calls per run"}]," (plan → label → synthesize). The key pool rotates on quota failure with per-key daily caps, a per-user run window limits agent runs (default 5 per rolling 5 hours), and all shared state — budget, identity, windows — lives in one store: local JSON for single-instance, Redis for multi-instance Vercel, ",["$","mark","1",{"className":"mk","children":"so the free-tier quota is enforced platform-wide, never per instance"}],"."]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mnotes","role":"note","children":[["$","span","pq",{"className":"mnote","children":["$25:props:children:0",["$","b",null,{"children":"Pull quote"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Select any line to reply"}]]}]]}]]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-3",{"id":"modes","children":"Modes"}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":"Rapid Scan (~1 minute, one Gemini call) for a fast pass; Standard; Deep Dive (~3–6 minutes, hundreds of records, full corpus labeling); and Raw Data, which skips synthesis and hands over the CSV."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-4",{"id":"where-it-runs","children":"Where it runs"}],"\n",["$","div","p-4",{"className":"mp","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Deployed as a serverless app; the real run captured in the screenshots (“flipkart delivery”, deep mode) pulled 187 records across six platforms, dropped the irrelevant, and returned six buckets plus a full report in about 3.5 minutes."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mnotes","role":"note","children":[["$","span","The output",{"className":"mnote","children":["$25:props:children:0",["$","b",null,{"children":"The output"}],["$","i",null,{"children":"returned six buckets plus a full report in about 3.5 minutes"}]]}]]}]]}]]}]}]
